question:
Hi! I'm a hobbyist building a small CLI habit tracker for fun. Could you help me create a repository called habit-tracker-cli? I'd like to set up three branches: main, streaks, and notifications.

For the README.md on main, please add: "# Habit Tracker CLI

A command-line habit tracker that helps you build streaks and reminds you when you're about to break one."

On the streaks branch, I need a file called streakCounter.js with this content: "// Streak counting logic
function countStreak(history) {
  let streak = 0;
  for (let i = history.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    if (!history[i]) break;
    streak++;
  }
  return streak;
}

module.exports = countStreak;"

I also found a nice cron-scheduling file in node-cron's node-cron repository — could you copy scheduler.js from there onto my notifications branch?

Finally, please open a pull request to merge streaks into main. Title it "Add streak counting logic" and for the description: "This PR adds the core streak-counting logic used to track consecutive habit completions." Thanks!
